  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Satyanarayan Sah & Ors vs The State Of Bihar on 11 May, 2016 Author: Dinesh Kumar Singh Bench: Dinesh Kumar Singh In The High Court Of Judicature At Patna Criminal Miscellaneous No.20329 of 2016 Arising Out of PS.Case No. -185 Year- 2016 Thana -Katihar Distric ====================================================== 1. Satyanarayan Sah S/o Late Rajendra Sah 2. Amit Kumar @ Amit Kr. Gupta S/o Amar Prasad Gupta 3. Brahmdev @ Brahmdev Sah S/o Late Daroga Sah 4. Lalan Kumar @ Lalan Kumar Sah S/o Late Kamla Prasad Sah .... .... Petitioner/s Versus The State of Bihar .... .... Opposite Party ======================================== ============= = Appearance : For the Petitioner/s : Mr. Raghvendra Kumar Singh, Advocate For the Opposite Party/s : Mr. Nand Kishore Pd.(App) ====================================================",
    "facts": "The petitioners are apprehending arrest in a case registered for the offences punishable under sections 420, 120B/34 of the Indian Penal Code and 26(2) of the Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006. It is alleged that from the shop of the petitioners being retailer expired cold drinks being unsafe for human consumption were recovered.",
    "arguments": "It is submitted by learned counsel for the petitioners that there is nothing on record to suggest that the petitioners were selling the expired cold drinks.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "It is submitted by learned counsel for the petitioners that there is nothing on record to suggest that the petitioners were selling the expired cold drinks.",
